    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "EDWARDS,\nMAR\n1\nEDW\n1954\nFORGE\nCommemorating\nthe first flight of the\nU.S. AIR FORCE\nXF-104\njet fighter built beg\nLOCKHEED\n+t\nГ\n2- PM\n5 Д\nAIR\nMAIL\nPROGRES\n50O POWERSON FLIGH\nSECURITY\nUNITED STATES POSTAGE\nVIA AIR MAIL\nHAROLD M. BIXBY, VICE PRES.\nPAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS, INC.\n135 EAST 42ND STREET\nNEW YORK, 17, N. X.",
      "Commemoraling\nthe first flight of the\nU.S. AIR FORCE\nXF -104\njel fighter built bag\nLOCKHEED\nLockheed takes pleasure in sending you this commemorative\ncachet which symbolizes another step in the advancement of\nmilitary aviation. For collectors, this envelope will have value\nas an authentic first flight cover. For others, it will serve as\nthe announcement of new progress in aviation.\nDue to security regulations it can be said only that the XF-104\nis the prototype of a new high speed, piloted air superiority\nfighter. Its simple concept insures that large numbers of the\nairplane can be made available and kept in combat readiness\nat all times."
    ],
